---
source: crates/leptoskit_cli/tests/snapshots.rs
expression: "normalize(&stdout(&output), &scratch.path)"
---
Runs a compiled test executable and retains its logs and JSON report

Usage: leptoskit test run [OPTIONS] --binary <BINARY> [-- <ARGS>...]

Arguments:
  [ARGS]...
          Arguments passed literally to the test executable, after --

Options:
      --binary <BINARY>
          Compiled executable for the selected target

      --platform <PLATFORM>
          Execution platform

          Possible values:
          - host:    The current host (macOS, Windows, or Linux)
          - ios:     An Apple simulator, selected by UDID
          - android: An Android device or emulator, selected by adb serial
          
          [default: host]

      --device <DEVICE>
          iOS simulator UDID or Android adb serial (required for mobile)

      --avd <AVD>
          Boot this installed Android AVD on the port in --device emulator-PORT

      --timeout <TIMEOUT>
          Deadline per setup, execution, or cleanup command, in seconds
          
          [default: 120]

      --artifacts <ARTIFACTS>
          Parent directory for a unique run's logs and report
          
          [default: target/leptoskit-tests]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
